{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> The sense: I will pay them recompense in full, for I love justice and hate robbery — even in an burnt offering that is offered before Me. Therefore, I will give their wage as their hire, like \"nor shall the wage of a hired worker remain\" (Leviticus 19:13):" "Now the sense of <b>robbery</b>: that I will not rob them — for if I do not give them their wage, I am robbing them of their hire:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 61, :notes {0 "The cited verse reference in the source text reads י\"ג י\"ח (Leviticus 19:18), but the phrase ולא תלין פעולת שכיר corresponds to Leviticus 19:13; corrected accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:37.193266526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}